    <section class="hero">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="emergency-icon">ALERT</div>
        <h1 class="headline">Emergency Services Left in the Dark</h1>
        <p class="subheadline">
          Council's secret Shore Road plans could put lives at risk - South West
          Ambulance Trust never consulted
        </p>
        <div class="byline">
          Investigation by North Swanage Traffic Concern Group • July 2025
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" id="revelation">
      <div class="narrow-container">
        <div class="chapter-number">Shocking Discovery</div>
        <h2 class="chapter-title">The Missing Consultation</h2>
        <div class="body-text">
          <p>
            <span class="drop-cap">W</span>hile Swanage Town Council pushes
            through their controversial Shore Road changes, we've uncovered a
            dangerous oversight: they NEVER consulted the South West Ambulance
            Trust about how emergency vehicles would access our community.
          </p>

          <p>
            That's right - NO ONE asked the ambulance service how their
            multi-million pound infrastructure plan would affect emergency
            response times to YOUR home, YOUR family, YOUR neighbors.
          </p>

          <p>
            But they did remember to design improvements that boost revenue to
            Council-owned assets. Priorities much?
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="sticky-stat">
      <div class="big-number">0</div>
      <div class="stat-label">Emergency Service Consultations</div>
      <div class="stat-description">
        Zero consultations with ambulance services during planning phase
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="consultation-void">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="void-stamp">VOID</div>
        <p class="void-text">
          Where public safety consultation should have been, there's nothing but
          dangerous negligence
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" id="consequences">
      <div class="narrow-container">
        <div class="chapter-number">The Consequences</div>
        <h2 class="chapter-title">Lives at Risk</h2>
        <div class="body-text">
          <p>
            Emergency response isn't a luxury - it's a lifeline. When Shore Road
            closes, ambulances will face the same traffic chaos as everyone
            else, navigating through congested Victorian streets never designed
            for emergency vehicles.
          </p>

          <p>
            The summer tourist season makes everything worse. When 180,000
            visitors flood Swanage, every minute counts. Blocked roads don't
            just cause inconvenience - they can be the difference between life
            and death.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="sticky-stat">
      <div class="big-number">?..</div>
      <div class="stat-label">Additional Minutes</div>
      <div class="stat-description">
        Unknown delay to emergency response times
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="impact-grid">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="impact-card">
          <div class="impact-icon">MEDICAL</div>
          <div class="impact-title">Medical Emergencies</div>
          <div class="impact-text">
            Heart attacks, strokes, and accidents require immediate response.
            Traffic delays can be fatal.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="impact-card">
          <div class="impact-icon">ELDERLY</div>
          <div class="impact-title">Elderly & Vulnerable</div>
          <div class="impact-text">
            Swanage's aging population depends on reliable emergency access more
            than ever.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="impact-card">
          <div class="impact-icon">FIRE</div>
          <div class="impact-title">Fire Services</div>
          <div class="impact-text">
            Fire engines and ambulances share the same congested alternative
            routes.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="priority-callout">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="priority-title">Public Safety Must Come First</h2>
        <p class="priority-text">
          Infrastructure decisions should protect lives, not endanger them. Any
          plan that affects emergency access MUST involve emergency services
          from day one. The fact that this didn't happen reveals a dangerous
          disregard for public safety.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="action-section">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 style="font-size: 36px; margin-bottom: 30px">
          Demand Emergency Service Consultation
        </h2>
        <p
          style="
            font-family: var(--sans);
            font-size: 18px;
            max-width: 600px;
            margin: 0 auto;
          "
        >
          Before any Shore Road changes proceed, emergency services MUST be
          properly consulted. Lives depend on it.
        </p>

        <div class="action-buttons">
          <a href="#" class="action-btn" onclick="shareEvidence()"
            >Share This Evidence</a
          >
          <a href="mailto:info@nstcg.org" class="action-btn">Email Concerns</a>
        </div>

        <div class="emergency-contact">
          <h3>Emergency Service Consultation Should Include:</h3>
          <p>
