    <!-- Chapter 2: The Problem -->
    <section class="chapter" id="problem">
      <div class="narrow-container">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 2</div>
        <h2 class="chapter-title">The Domino Effect</h2>
        <div class="body-text">
          <p>
            When Shore Road closes, 8,000 daily vehicle movements don't simply
            vanish. They cascade through residential streets never designed for
            such volume, creating a domino effect of congestion, delays, and
            safety hazards.
          </p>

          <p>
            Our analysis of traffic modeling data reveals a troubling picture:
            narrow Victorian-era streets facing modern traffic loads they cannot
            sustain. Emergency response times stretched beyond safe limits.
            School children navigating increasingly dangerous crossings.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="sticky-stat">
        <div class="big-number">47</div>
        <p>Minutes added to peak-hour emergency response times</p>
      </div>

      <div class="narrow-container">
        <div class="body-text">
          <p>
            The summer tourist season amplifies every problem. In August 2023,
            Swanage welcomed 180,000 visitors. Without Shore Road, their
            vehicles will flood through residential neighborhoods, turning quiet
            streets into parking lots.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
